/-!
# Stabilizer-chain certificates

Verified data for the cardinality route with base `22, 0, 1, 2, 5, 3`:

* the orbit of `22` has size `23` (powers of the 23-cycle `m23c`);
* the stabilizer of `22` has orbit size `22` on `0`;
* the stabilizer of `22,0` has orbit size `21` on `1`;
* the stabilizer of `22,0,1` has orbit size `20` on `2`;
* the stabilizer of `22,0,1,2` moves `5` through the 16 points outside the
  block `B0 = {0,1,2,3,4,21,22}` (which it preserves);
* the stabilizer of `22,0,1,2,5` moves `3` through the 3 points
  `{3,4,21} = B0 \ {0,1,2,22}`;
* the stabilizer of `22,0,1,2,5,3` is trivial (`FinalStabilizer.lean`).

The words for the levels below the first are the `M22` stabilizer-chain
words, reused verbatim: the generators `m23a`, `m23b` act on `0,…,21`
exactly as `m22a`, `m22b` do and fix the new point `22`.

No external computation is trusted here until it is represented as data and
checked by Lean.
-/

namespace CFSG.Certificates.Mathieu23
namespace M23Certificates
namespace StabilizerChain

open SteinerSystem

/-- The product of the target stabilizer-chain indices. -/
theorem target_index_product : 23 * 22 * 21 * 20 * 16 * 3 = 10200960 := by
  norm_num

/-- First-step words: `levelOneWord x` sends `22` to `x` (powers of `m23c`). -/
def levelOneWord (x : Fin 23) : Word :=
  match x.val with
  | 0 => List.replicate 10 Gen.cInv
  | 1 => [Gen.c]
  | 2 => List.replicate 9 Gen.cInv
  | 3 => List.replicate 6 Gen.cInv
  | 4 => List.replicate 7 Gen.c
  | 5 => List.replicate 7 Gen.cInv
  | 6 => List.replicate 5 Gen.cInv
  | 7 => List.replicate 3 Gen.c
  | 8 => List.replicate 3 Gen.cInv
  | 9 => List.replicate 10 Gen.c
  | 10 => List.replicate 6 Gen.c
  | 11 => List.replicate 2 Gen.cInv
  | 12 => List.replicate 11 Gen.c
  | 13 => List.replicate 5 Gen.c
  | 14 => List.replicate 4 Gen.cInv
  | 15 => List.replicate 9 Gen.c
  | 16 => [Gen.cInv]
  | 17 => List.replicate 8 Gen.cInv
  | 18 => List.replicate 4 Gen.c
  | 19 => List.replicate 11 Gen.cInv
  | 20 => List.replicate 8 Gen.c
  | 21 => List.replicate 2 Gen.c
  | _ => []

/-- Second-step words: fix `22`, send `0` to `x` (the `M22` first-step words). -/
